 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast-doubling Fibonacci mod 1_000_000_007. It walks the bits of n from the top, using one modulo per multiplication and letting Python's % handle the negative 2b-a term. It reads one integer per line from stdin and prints fib(n) mod 1e9+7. It matches the sample output (in-0/out-0) byte for byte, and fib(10) prints 55. The latest variant was adopted after a +6% win (medians 2.606 to 2.765), and the assay registered a baseline of 2.61669 with 2.6% noise. I'm stopping here: the NEED is met and further tuning would likely fall under the 3% win threshold.",
